350
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:46,800
So we had, it was, it was a great, that was a great introduction.

351
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:47,800
That's awesome.

352
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:55,480
And I know we were texting before I came over and there were three, you filtered down to

353
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:58,920
two, there were three questions you were going to ask people in the different Concords.

354
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:04,280
I want to ask them to you about Concord, Massachusetts.

355
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:07,680
What's the best part about living in Concord, Massachusetts?

356
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:09,480
Let me go back a step.

357
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,480
Okay.

358
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:12,480
Just tell you a little bit about why I asked these questions.

359
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:19,840
And then I'll answer the question because I was thinking about that myself.

360
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:22,360
Because of the randomness of the project, right?

361
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:23,360
Yeah.

362
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:28,800
There's nothing that really connects things, all these things together.

363
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:36,560
My daughter, who's a sociologist said, you have to have some definitive questions that

364
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:38,360
you ask everybody.

365
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:44,760
And that'll help you filter out or group together different ideas and different themes.

366
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:55,080
So much of the country, you can see why people are frustrated and why people are upset.

367
00:20:55,080 --> 00:21:00,360
You go out to some of these places and you can find the falling down barns.

368
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:02,480
You can see the rusted out cars.

369
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:08,580
You can see needles in the street, that kind of thing.

370
00:21:08,580 --> 00:21:11,080
You can see the signs of why life is tough.

371
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,080
Yep.

372
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:22,480
And I would say maybe three quarters of the places I've been to had better days.

373
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,760
Sure.

374
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:28,400
One quarter of them are doing well or actually life is getting better.

375
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:32,240
But I would say at least three quarters of them are, life is getting worse.

376
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:39,880
So I really decided I have to try and find the things that are good about these places,

377
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:42,200
and joyful about these places.

378
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,640
So I always start off with that question.

379
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:48,000
What's the best part about living in your Concord?

380
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:55,400
And that generally gives them an opportunity to find something that's optimistic about

381
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:56,400
